Pump Technology Watch: Materials and Application-Specific Designs Expand Adoption
AODD pump technology is evolving through improvements in diaphragm materials and application-specific engineering. PTFE and Santoprene have enhanced chemical resistance and durability, while PVDF and PE are gaining attention for demanding corrosive environments.

Manufacturers are also developing specialized designs for individual industries. Food and beverage users require sanitary configurations, while pharmaceutical facilities emphasize sterile designs and reduced dead zones. Modular pump systems can provide greater flexibility when equipment is used across multiple industrial applications.

